{
  "name": "OPS.SLK-D Backfill Slack IDs",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## OPS.SLK-D · Backfill Slack IDs\n\nFor people who were ALREADY in Slack when their team_members row was created — team_join never fired for them, so slack_user_id is null and they were never provisioned.\n\nRuns hourly + on demand. Finds unlinked non-departed members, looks each up in Slack by email, writes slack_user_id, then provisions: role channels plus the watcher fan-out (watch_scope 'all' = every channel, 'rep_channels' = every market sales channel).\n\nSafe to re-run. already_in_channel counts as success. Respects SLACK_ONBOARDING_MODE — anything but 'live' is shadow: it links the Slack ID but performs no invites.\n\nusers_not_found just means they have not joined Slack yet — skipped silently, picked up on a later run.\n\n2026-09-11 — POSTS ONLY ON CHANGE. Watchers are re-checked every hour on purpose (so they land in new channels), but a card is posted only when someone is newly linked, Slack actually adds someone to a channel, an invite fails, or a planning alert appears. Identical alert text is posted at most once per 24h. The hourly 'nothing to do' card was removed.\n\n2026-09-14 — PER-REP CHANNELS REMOVED. Reps live in #sales-<market>; nothing here creates or joins a private per-rep channel any more.",
        "height": 560,
        "width": 620,
        "color": 4
      },
